look like, at a high level (rough, please cross-check):

```
if gate-enabled && scope == nil {
	// error: required value
} else if scope != nil {
	// if we get here, the gate may or may not be enabled, but scope has a value.
	if not valid scope value
		// error: not supported
	} else {
	    // if we get here, we have a valid scope.
	    if scope == cluster
		    if namespace != nil {
			    // error: forbidden when scope is cluster
		    }
	    }
	    if scope == Namespace {
		    if namespace == nil {
			    // error: required when scope is NS
		    }
	   }
	}
}
```

Then, when we eventually remove the gate, it's simply removing the outermost
if/else.

Does that make sense?

Great timing. I was just working on this logic and I arrived close to where you are.
We can't use `else if` because in that case, when gate is enabled and a value is set (to anything), the majority of validation will be skipped.


This is what I've right now (added comments here, not in git patch):
```go
        // when gate goes away, we have to delete the first condition of this if block
        if utilfeature.DefaultFeatureGate.Enabled(features.IngressClassNamespacedParams) && params.Scope == nil {
                allErrs = append(allErrs, field.Required(fldPath.Child("scope"), "scope is required"))
                return allErrs
        }
        // need to check for namespace too because if scope is not set, but namespace is we still validate
        if params.Scope != nil || params.Namespace != nil {
                scope := utilpointer.StringPtrDerefOr(params.Scope, "")
                namespace := utilpointer.StringPtrDerefOr(params.Namespace, "")
 
                if !supportedIngressClassParametersReferenceScopes.Has(scope) {
                        allErrs = append(allErrs, field.NotSupported(fldPath.Child("scope"), scope,
                                supportedIngressClassParametersReferenceScopes.List()))
                } else {

                        if scope == networking.IngressClassParametersReferenceScopeNamespace {
                                if namespace == "" {
                                        allErrs = append(allErrs, field.Required(fldPath.Child("namespace"), "namespace is required when spec.parameters.scope is set to Namespace"))
                                } else {
                                       // performs namespace validation only when needed
                                        for _, msg := range apivalidation.ValidateNamespaceName(namespace, false) {
                                                allErrs = append(allErrs, field.Invalid(fldPath.Child("namespace"), namespace, msg))
                                        }
                                }
                        }

                        if scope == networking.IngressClassParametersReferenceScopeCluster && namespace != "" {
                                allErrs = append(allErrs, field.Forbidden(fldPath.Child("namespace"), "namespace is forbidden when spec.parameters.scope is set to Cluster"))
                        }
                }
        }
```

How does that sound?
